{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfUcT5ozotf9DuEP4TC2k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing further is needed — the deliverable is complete and verified, so there are no remaining items to request.\n\n## Final summary\n\n**Deliverable:** `/app/estimator.py` (225 lines, standard library only, no numpy) — syntax-checked and confirmed intact.\n\n**Approach:**\n- Splits each arena into 16 cells: (topic, length) stratum × judge verdict. The judge's share of each cell is free; the unknowns are the judge's per-cell precision (`P(true win | judge win)`) and `P(true win | judge loss)`, which is exactly where the judge's directional bias lives.\n- Spends the 220-label budget on random prompts *within* those cells using Neyman allocation weighted by `env.production_mix` (read at run time, never hardcoded), so heavily-weighted production strata get more labels.\n- Each cell gets a Beta posterior (Jeffreys + a weak 3-pseudo-observation prior from 192 dev-arena labels I bought in the lab). The production-mix win rate posterior is simulated (6000 draws) and the interval taken from its quantiles, slightly widened beyond the 90% nominal level so 24 arenas clear the 80% coverage bar with margin.\n\n**Validation:**\n- Mock simulator (with the judge error rates perturbed by up to ±30% to guard against over-fitting the lab priors): coverage 0.97–0.98, mean width ≈ 0.08–0.09 (cap is 0.17), bias ≈ 0.\n- Edge cases (missing stratum, single stratum, budget 0/1/5/40, 100-prompt arena) all run and submit.\n- `lab dry_run` on `dev2`: point 0.597, interval [0.552, 0.638], width 0.087, no errors.\n\nLab budget: 204/220 used (16 left, intentionally unspent). The task instructed to write, dry-run, then stop — done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":498,"cache_read_input_tokens":29605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_in